\date{2024-09-16}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\taxon{Definition}
\import{common}
\title{Right adjoint left inverses}

\p{
 Given a pair of converse maps #{L : X \leftrightarrow Y : R}, we say #{R} is a \concept{right adjoint left inverse} to #{L} if it is a [right adjoint](stt-0033) to #{L} and the unit is a natural isomorphism.
}

\p{Under appropriate completeness conditions, #{R} is therefore a retraction of #{L}. For the remainder of this note, we may for this reason assume #{R} is a retraction of #{L}, with the understanding that this may be an evil notion in the absence of the appropriate completeness conditions.}
